# <<TOPIC>>.harness

<<TOPIC_BLURB>>

This is a *reference / discussion harness* — it bundles the literature library (`.knowledge/`), project notes, and the Zulip bridge to the `<<ZULIP_STREAM>>` stream on <<ZULIP_SITE>>. Implementation code lives elsewhere.

## Getting started

Open [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) in any directory and paste:

```
clone https://github.com/<<GITHUB_REMOTE>> and invoke the onboard skill.
```

The project-level `onboard` skill (in `.claude/skills/onboard/`) handles plugin install on first run — it edits your `~/.claude/settings.json` to enable the [`zlp-harness`](https://github.com/GiggleLiu/zlp-harness) plugin, asks you to restart Claude Code, then on the second invocation delegates to the plugin's `zlp-onboard` skill. That flow shows where to download `zuliprc` from <<ZULIP_SITE>>, creates the local credential directory, places the file there, verifies the bridge with `make zulip-whoami`, syncs Zulip messages into `.zulip/`, recommends adding key references with `download-ref`, and helps define reliable update sources in `CLAUDE.md` for `zlp-advisor`.

For everything else (commands, knowledge base layout, adding references, posting to Zulip), see [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md).
